Host-side render harness for GameTitleActivity (the "LETHALITY UNRATED" cert
screen). Not a gtest suite (see test/README for those) -- this compiles the
REAL, unmodified GameTitleActivity draw calls against the REAL font/renderer
pipeline and dumps the actual framebuffer to an image, so a layout change can
be verified pixel-by-pixel instead of by eyeballing device coordinates in
source.

Why not gtest/CMake: GameTitleActivity pulls in the full GfxRenderer/EpdFont/
Activity dependency graph, most of which has Arduino/FreeRTOS/SPI coupling
that the existing CMake test targets don't need to touch. Same standalone-
g++ technique as test/game_save/GameSaveRoundTripHarness.cpp.

## Build

Object files persist in /tmp/objs/ across sessions -- only recompile what
changed, then always do a fresh full link (cheap, and avoids stale-.o bugs).

  INCLUDES="-include Arduino.h \
    -I test/game_title_render/stubs \
    -I test/game_title_render/mirror/src \
    -I test/game_title_render/mirror/src/activities \
    -I test/game_title_render/mirror/src/activities/game \
    -I src -I src/game \
    -I lib/EpdFont/builtinFonts -I lib/EpdFont -I lib/Epub -I lib/FsHelpers \
    -I lib/GfxRenderer -I lib/I18n -I lib/InflateReader -I lib/JpegToBmpConverter \
    -I lib/JsonParser -I lib/KOReaderSync -I lib/Logging -I lib/Memory \
    -I lib/MiniBidi -I lib/OpdsParser -I lib/Serialization -I lib/Txt -I lib/Utf8 \
    -I lib/XmlParserUtils -I lib/Xtc -I lib/ZipFile -I lib/expat -I lib/hal \
    -I lib/miniz -I lib/uzlib -I lib/uzlib/src"

  mkdir -p /tmp/objs
  for src in \
      test/game_title_render/GameTitleRenderHarness.cpp \
      test/game_title_render/mirror/src/activities/game/GameTitleActivity.cpp \
      test/game_title_render/mirror/src/activities/Activity.cpp \
      lib/GfxRenderer/GfxRenderer.cpp \
      lib/GfxRenderer/Bitmap.cpp \
      lib/GfxRenderer/BitmapHelpers.cpp \
      lib/GfxRenderer/FontCacheManager.cpp \
      lib/EpdFont/EpdFont.cpp \
      lib/EpdFont/EpdFontFamily.cpp \
      lib/EpdFont/FontDecompressor.cpp \
      lib/EpdFont/SdCardFont.cpp \
      lib/InflateReader/InflateReader.cpp \
      lib/Utf8/Utf8.cpp \
      lib/MiniBidi/BidiUtils.cpp \
      lib/Memory/BuildScratch.cpp \
      ; do
    obj=/tmp/objs/$(basename "${src%.*}" | tr 'A-Z' 'a-z').o
    g++ -std=c++20 -O2 -Wall -Wextra $INCLUDES -c "$src" -o "$obj"
  done

  # These three are plain C, not C++ -- compile with gcc, not g++:
  #  - tinflate.c: void*->unsigned char* implicit conversions are C-legal, not C++-legal.
  #  - uzlib_checksum_stub.c: same TU family as tinflate.c, same reason.
  #  - minibidi.c: BidiUtils.cpp links against its bidi_class/do_bidi/do_shape as C symbols
  #    (unmangled). g++ would compile it fine but name-mangle those symbols as C++, and the
  #    link then fails with "undefined reference to bidi_class" etc -- discovered by actually
  #    doing a from-scratch verification build of this recipe, not by inspection.
  gcc -O2 -I test/game_title_render/stubs -I lib/uzlib -I lib/uzlib/src \
    -c lib/uzlib/src/tinflate.c -o /tmp/objs/tinflate.o
  gcc -O2 -I test/game_title_render/stubs -I lib/uzlib -I lib/uzlib/src \
    -c test/game_title_render/stubs/uzlib_checksum_stub.c -o /tmp/objs/uzlib_checksum_stub.o
  gcc -O2 -I lib/MiniBidi -c lib/MiniBidi/minibidi.c -o /tmp/objs/minibidi.o

  g++ /tmp/objs/*.o -o /tmp/game_title_render_harness

## Run

  /tmp/game_title_render_harness /tmp/game_title.pgm
  python3 /tmp/pgm_to_png.py /tmp/game_title.pgm /tmp/game_title.png

(pgm_to_png.py is a throwaway ~50-line P5->PNG encoder, struct+zlib only, no
external image lib dependency -- recreate it if /tmp has been wiped; there's
nothing to it beyond a PGM header parse and a minimal PNG chunk writer.)

## Why mirror/ exists, and why it's symlinks

test/game_title_render/mirror/src/... are symlinks back to the real src/...
tree, not copies. The harness compiles GameTitleActivity.cpp and Activity.cpp
through this mirror path (rather than -I src directly for those two files)
so their #include "GameActivity.h" / #include "ActivityManager.h" etc.
resolve against local stub headers co-located in the mirror tree
(mirror/src/activities/game/GameActivity.h, mirror/src/activities/
ActivityManager.h, mirror/src/activities/RenderLock.h, mirror/src/game/
GameState.h) instead of the real headers, without editing or forking the
real .cpp files at all -- the .cpp compiled is byte-identical to the real
source because it IS the real source, just reached through a symlink.

Because these are symlinks, `diff`/`find` following them will make mirror/
and src/ look like identical trees -- they are, deliberately. Don't delete
mirror/ thinking it's a stale duplicate.

## Font registration

Register every font+style GameTitleActivity actually draws with, matching
src/main.cpp's setupDisplayAndFonts() exactly:
  - UI_10_FONT_ID, UI_12_FONT_ID: both REGULAR and BOLD faces. Several draw
    calls (HUD blocks, cert line) use EpdFontFamily::BOLD -- registering only
    REGULAR silently renders/measures the wrong glyphs with no error.
  - NOTOSANS_16_FONT_ID: REGULAR only (nothing on this screen uses it bold).
  - SMALL_FONT_ID (notosans_8_regular): added for the cert line fix, 2026-08.
    Already used elsewhere (BootActivity, SleepActivity, FileBrowserActivity,
    CalibreConnectActivity, CrossPointWebServerActivity) -- not a new font
    asset. If a future change needs a font not yet registered here, check
    src/main.cpp's setupDisplayAndFonts() for the real registration and add
    the matching insertFont() call, don't guess at a substitute.

A FontDecompressor + FontCacheManager must be wired to the renderer before
render() runs, or every glyph bitmap comes back null silently (no crash, no
error -- just blank text). See GameTitleRenderHarness.cpp's own comments for
the exact call sequence.

## HalDisplay stub

test/game_title_render/stubs/HalDisplay.h reports the PHYSICAL panel size
(800x480), not the logical portrait canvas (480x800) GameTitleActivity draws
into -- GfxRenderer::begin() reads this as panelWidth/panelHeight and uses it
to rotate logical draw coordinates into physical ones. Reporting the logical
size here (a real mistake made once) feeds GfxRenderer a panel it thinks is
already portrait-shaped, so its own rotation then computes physical
coordinates outside the real bounds ("Outside range" log spam, and a wrong
image). The harness's PGM writer un-rotates the physical buffer back to
logical 480x800 on the way out, so the dumped image reads right-side-up.

## Verifying a layout change -- do this every time, not just when it looks wrong

Trusting a font's getFontAscenderSize() (or eyeballing the PNG) is not
sufficient -- during the cert-line fix (2026-08-15) both misled the fix by a
few pixels in ways only pixel measurement caught. Use both of the following
on the rendered PGM/PNG before calling a layout change done:

1. Row-by-row pixel density scan: for the y-range around the change, count
   dark pixels (<128) across a fixed x-range per row. Full-width counts
   (~390+ on this 480-wide canvas) are borders/rules; moderate/varying counts
   are letter ink; a count of 0 is a genuinely clear row. Confirm at least
   one fully-clear row exists between the new element and every neighboring
   element it must not touch.

2. Connected-component (flood-fill) analysis over the affected bounding box:
   BFS/queue-based 8-connected flood fill to enumerate distinct ink blobs.
   If the new text's blob has merged with a border's or another element's
   blob (same component, spanning both), the row-density scan's "clear row"
   reading was misleading (e.g. anti-aliasing) -- treat a merge as a fail
   regardless of what the density scan showed.

Only call a layout fix verified once both checks agree, on the actual
rendered output of the real draw calls -- not the same GfxRenderer helper
computing a metric that might be wrong.

## Reference: the cert-line fix (2026-08-15)

Worked example of the above: LETHALITY UNRATED at UI_12/baseline=494
collided with the tick ring (drawTickRing, starts y=475) and, once dropped a
size, the wordmark's own outer border (drawRect, bottoms out y=459) --
leaving only a 16px clear band (y459-y475) for the whole line. Switched to
SMALL_FONT_ID (already-registered, no new font asset) and picked
baseline=473 by measuring the string's REAL ink extent in isolation (~12px
cap-height above baseline for an all-caps string, not the font's reported
18px ascender) rather than trusting getFontAscenderSize() directly. Verified
clear of both neighbors by both techniques above before shipping. See
src/activities/game/GameTitleActivity.cpp's kCertFontId/render() comments
for the full numeric trail.
